{"ratings":[{"id":"C1","consequence":"outage","trigger":"plausible","reason":"Restoring a model with incompatible saved settings is accepted but prevents the daemon from starting on restart."},{"id":"C2","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"Restoring a compatible model clears the warning while routing silently continues using the fallback until restart."},{"id":"C3","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A bare IPv6 remote host causes all local management actions to fail before SSH runs."},{"id":"C4","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A tunneled or aliased provider can be reported unreachable and left disabled because the health probe uses the wrong endpoint without its key."},{"id":"C5","consequence":"resume","trigger":"plausible","reason":"An interrupted historical evaluation containing a retired model cannot resume, including its unfinished work for available models."},{"id":"C7","consequence":"diag","trigger":"unusual","reason":"A persisted provider preference containing a live model ID is reported as absent from the catalog instead of being identified as a model ID."},{"id":"C9","consequence":"outage","trigger":"plausible","reason":"The reproduced validation gap is the same as C1 and can leave the daemon unable to start after a catalog addition."},{"id":"C4b","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A bare IPv6 remote host makes URL construction throw before any remote management action reaches SSH."},{"id":"C5b","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"Retrying a historical run with a retired model in its saved chain is refused before an available fallback can be used."}]}